1***********************************************************************************************************************************
 *                    EOS3: EQUATION OF STATE FOR WATER-AIR MIXTURES                                                               *
 ***********************************************************************************************************************************


    OPTIONS SELECTED ARE: (NK,NEQ,NPH,NB) = (2,3,2, 6)

                           NK  =  2   - NUMBER OF FLUID COMPONENTS
                           NEQ =  3   - NUMBER OF EQUATIONS PER GRID BLOCK
                           NPH =  2   - NUMBER OF PHASES THAT CAN BE PRESENT
                           NB  =  6   - NUMBER OF SECONDARY PARAMETERS (OTHER THAN COMPONENT MASS FRACTIONS)

                   For NK = 2 and NB = 8, diffusion is "on", otherwise, diffusion is "off"


   AVAILABLE OPTIONS ARE: (NK,NEQ,NPH,NB) = (2,3,2,6) - WATER AND AIR, NON-ISOTHERMAL
                                            (2,3,2,8) - WATER AND AIR, NON-ISOTHERMAL, DIFFUSION
                                            (2,2,2,6) - WATER AND AIR, ISOTHERMAL
                                            (2,2,2,8) - WATER AND AIR, ISOTHERMAL, DIFFUSION

 ***********************************************************************************************************************************


 THE PRIMARY VARIABLES ARE
  P - PRESSURE           D - DENSITYT - TEMPERATURE         X - AIR MASS FRACTION         S+10. - (GAS PHASE SATURATION + 10.)

 _______________________________________________________

     PHASE CONDITION               PRIMARY VARIABLES
 _______________________________________________________

     SINGLE-PHASE GAS                P,     X, T

     SINGLE-PHASE LIQUID             P,     X, T

     TWO-PHASE                       P, S+10., T

     SUPERCRITICAL                   D,     X, T

 _______________________________________________________


 ***********************************************************************************************************************************

 CHOICES BY WAY OF THE MOP-ARRAY ARE AS FOLLOWS.

 MOP(19) = 0 *** ALLOWS INITIALIZATION WITH DIFFERENT SETS OF PRIMARY VARIABLES.
         = 0: (P,X,T) FOR SINGLE PHASE, (P,S+10,T) FOR TWO-PHASE         = 1: (P,T,X) FOR SINGLE PHASE, (P,S,T) FOR TWO-PHASE (AS IN THE TOUGH CODE)

..... NEGLECT VAPOR PRESSURE LOWERING .....                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 

